Purpose: hooks for `zinc profile <file> --engine quickjs` (ZN-598): an opcode histogram in the dispatch macro, a call hook at bytecode
  function entry, a backward-jump hook on goto (loop iterations), a hook when a function's bytecode is freed, and JS_ZnProfCurrent /
  JS_ZnProfDescribe so a SIGPROF sampler can name the running bytecode function (a method or an arrow by its "name" property;
  src/qjs/qjs_prof.cpp). Everything is under #ifdef ZN_QJS_PROFILE (CMake option, off by default).
Measured: zero cost when off: quickjs.c compiled with zn_quickjs's flags (-O2) gives the same instructions as the v0.17.0 release
  (otool -tv, 207,986 lines; only the __LINE__ constants of the shifted lines and the rip offsets differ; __text 788,478 bytes both).
  SWITCH keeps the release's form when off, so other compilers and -O0 builds compile the release's dispatch too.
Upstream: not upstreamable: a Zinc-specific profiler interface into the interpreter's private frames.
